        "body": "## Description\r\n\r\nAdd efficient clear() method implementations to all cache classes (Cache, FIFOCache, LFUCache, LRUCache, RRCache, TTLCache, TLRUCache) that directly clear internal data structures instead of relying on the default MutableMapping.clear() which calls popitem() recursively.\r\n\r\n## Motivation and Context\r\n\r\nThe default MutableMapping.clear() implementation calls popitem() in a loop until the cache is empty, resulting in O(n) complexity. For large caches, this becomes a significant performance bottleneck. \r\n\r\nIn my use case, I have a cache for Elasticsearch queries which stores +400k objects and gets cleared after the search is completed. The recursive popitem() approach was consuming too much time, making the clear operation a bottleneck in the data pipeline.\r\n\r\nWhile this can be addressed by creating a new cache object, clear() is typically expected to be a fast O(1) operation in most data structures. The unexpected O(n) behavior made this performance issue difficult to identify and debug.\r\n\r\nThe new implementation directly clears the internal data structures (__data, __order, __links, etc.) in O(1) time, providing a substantial performance improvement for large caches.\r\n\r\n## Has this been tested and documented?\r\n* Added test_clear, test_clear_empty, and test_clear_getsizeof to CacheTestMixin (runs for all cache types)\r\n* Added test_lru_clear to verify LRU order tracking is reset after clear\r\n* Added test_lfu_clear to verify LFU frequency tracking is reset after clear\r\n",
